Mesa Wayland WSI: serialize automatic FIFO targets in the compositor clock.

The swapchain's target bookkeeping is in its own time domain (normally
CLOCK_MONOTONIC). wp_commit_timer_v1.set_timestamp requires the compositor's
presentation clock, which Weston X11 may advertise as CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW.
Reuse Mesa's existing reverse conversion only at the automatic FIFO handover;
application-provided absolute timing is already converted by its setter.

Fixes: 660136d8abe7cf6997168c174f82adb59c47f0d4
Upstream source: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/blob/mesa-26.2.2/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_wayland.c
Protocol: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/wayland/wayland-protocols/-/blob/main/staging/commit-timing/commit-timing-v1.xml

--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_wayland.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_wayland.c
@@ -3259,5 +3259,8 @@
       /* Take back 500 us as a safety margin, to ensure we don't miss our
        * target due to round-off error.
        */
-      timespec_from_nsec(&target_ts, target - 500000);
+      /* Keep prediction in swapchain time, but serialize the constraint in
+       * the compositor's presentation clock domain. */
+      timespec_from_nsec(&target_ts,
+                        wsi_wl_convert_wayland_to_swapchain_time(chain, target - 500000, true));
    }
